/// Requests “Always” location authorization from the user.
/// Call this method to prompt the user to grant “Always” access to location services, which is required for the SDK to operate optimally in the background.
/// This is typically needed for continuous tracking, background events, and ensuring reliable trip detection even when the app is not in the foreground.
/// important:
/// Ensure that your app includes the appropriate usage descriptions (<code>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</code> and <code>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</code>)
/// in its Info.plist, or the system prompt will not be displayed and location authorization will be denied.
/// note:
/// The exact system prompt and flow depend on the current authorization status and platform version.
/// seealso:
/// <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/corelocation/requesting_authorization_for_location_services">Apple Developer Documentation: Requesting Authorization for Location Services</a>
- (void)requestLocationAlwaysPermission;
